# Digests the transpiler recognises its modelled capabilities by.
#
# A capability here is a declaration the transpiler models exactly rather than
# generically: a configure-style build, a Python generator, a Mesa or Nouveau
# lane. Modelling one means reproducing decisions that live in the mmakefile,
# the source manifests and a driver script, so it is only sound for the inputs
# that were read. Each capability is therefore gated on a digest of those
# inputs, and fails closed: a changed input means the capability is not
# recognised and the declaration lands in the unmodelled report.
#
# Every deliberate change to one of these files needs a new value here. The
# failure names the file and, where the digest is of a text block rather than a
# whole file, prints the digest it computed. Re-pin from that rather than by
# hand.
#
# The values live in this file and not in `.rs` constants because they are data
# about the tree: they change on a different schedule than the code that reads
# them, they were spelled three times over for one archive, and while they sat
# in `parser.rs` every re-pin was a code edit in the 12 000-line file the
# decomposition has to split. See OPEN-POINTS 46, and 7 for the same move in
# aros-verify.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In-tree inputs of a modelled capability
#
# Checked against the tree being transpiled. Three of them are also emitted
# into the generated CMake, so the build re-checks the same bytes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# tools/ADFlib/adflib-configure.inputs
adflib-configure-manifest = a63a7498752d68175093b94dba873cc8a343d75179feec5cd6a6020e56e779a5

# workbench/network/WirelessManager/wirelessmanager-configure.inputs
